# Build artifacts
/koc
koc-linux-*
koc-darwin-*
koc-windows-*
/dist/
*.sha256
*.test
*.out
*.prof
# Root-anchored: an unanchored "coverage.*" also swallowed docs/coverage.md.
# Generated coverage profiles land at the repo root; *.out/*.prof cover the rest.
/coverage.*

# Editor / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Local credentials — never commit
clouds.yaml
secure.yaml
/completions/

# Key material and credential files — never commit.
#
# The project's own docs tell operators to create some of these IN the working
# tree: `koc vault kv export --help` and README "Encrypted Vault export" say to
# run `openssl genrsa -out koc-export.key 4096` and write the report to
# .junit/vault.xml. Without these lines a single `git add -A` publishes the
# export identity's PRIVATE key to a public repository.
*.key
*.pem
*.crt
*.cer
*.csr
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
koc-export.*
# openrc / kubeconfig files pasted in for a quick check against a real cloud
openrc
*.openrc
*openrc.sh
kubeconfig
*.kubeconfig

# Encrypted-export reports (contain real Vault paths even when payloads are
# sealed) and other local test-report output.
.junit/

# Supply-chain artifacts produced locally by goreleaser/syft/cosign; the
# release versions live on the GitHub Release, never in git.
*.sbom.json
*.spdx.json
*.sig

